From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] composite-blit: build under -Werror=format-security

0027's decline() logs its reason through a generic lambda, so the
reasons without arguments instantiate infof( pszReason ) -- a
non-literal format with no arguments, which makepkg's
-Werror=format-security turns into an error:

  rendervulkan.cpp:4764:37: error: format not a string literal and no
  format arguments [-Werror=format-security]

ROCKNIX builds without that flag. Route the argument-less
instantiations through "%s"; the others are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
index 3740a92..a6b4eb9 100644
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -4761,7 +4761,11 @@ static bool vulkan_composite_blit( CVulkanCmdBuffer *cmdBuffer, const struct Fra
 		if ( !( s_uLoggedReasons & ( 1u << uBit ) ) )
 		{
 			s_uLoggedReasons |= 1u << uBit;
-			vk_log.infof( pszReason, args... );
+			// -Werror=format-security (makepkg's CFLAGS) rejects a non-literal format with no arguments
+			if constexpr ( sizeof...( args ) == 0 )
+				vk_log.infof( "%s", pszReason );
+			else
+				vk_log.infof( pszReason, args... );
 		}
 		return false;
 	};
